        "original_id": "334834d7-3862-57b1-aab5-68fc46ce02e8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Abraham \"Abe\" Weinberg, Dutch Schultz, Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll, Jack \"Legs\" Diamond, Salvatore Maranzano\n- Events: Manhattan Bootleg Wars, gangland slayings\n- Places: New York City\n- Topics: organized crime, mob hitmen\n\nFacts:\n- Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll, born Uinseann Ó Colla, was born on July 20, 1908.\n- Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll was an Irish American mob hitman active in New York City during the 1920s and early 1930s.\n- Abraham \"Abe\" Weinberg became one of Dutch Schultz's top gunmen during the Manhattan Bootleg Wars.\n- Abraham \"Abe\" Weinberg was later a suspect in the high-profile gangland slayings of Jack \"Legs\" Diamond, Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll, and Salvatore Maranzano.\n- Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll died on February 7, 1932.",
